          "filename": "Fort Omdurman (302).png",
          "caption": "Sketch by C.G. Gordon to illustrate the following scene:\nNovember 14: The Omdurman Fort is ill placed, as it cannot see the ground down to the river, and is distant 1200 yards from the river. The Arabs on left bank of the White Nile opposite the Husseinyeh number 500 (I expect all are my soldiers), and they are so far away from any reserve that it would be easy to crush them before they were aided, if we dared to try, which we do no not.",
